"""HSK 6 readings 5–8: rehearsal, work trials and a misplaced manuscript."""
import sys
from bag_reading_edits import apply_bag_edits
from advanced_reading_repair import apply
EDITS={
5:{'-d':{
21:('慢一点也能唱出感觉啊。先唱清，再试别的唱法。',"You can still make it expressive more slowly. Get it clear first, then try other ways."),
23:('好，唱完听听哪里不一样。两遍都录下来吧。',"Okay, let's hear what's different afterwards. Let's record both takes.")},
'-r':{
5:('有一遍我漏了留，只唱你把风给我，听着还像一句完整的话，当时没发现。林安把原稿放到我面前，用笔点着那个字，让我先读留给我。我读完又试着唱，到了那个位置，眼睛还在看纸，音乐已经过去了。我们只放这一小段，慢一点再来，终于把字接上。她说这回听见留了，我笑着问那风是不是也真的留下来了。',"In one take I missed 留 and sang 'you give me the wind'; it still sounded like a complete sentence. Lin An pointed to 留 on the lyric sheet and had me read 留给我 first. Singing again, I was still looking at the paper when the music went past. We slowed just that short section and finally fitted the word in. She could hear 留 this time; I joked whether the wind had really stayed too."),
6:('节奏快起来以后，屏幕上一行已经换掉，我却还唱到中间。林安按停音乐，让我从没说完的话那一行再来。我把那一行读完，指着纸说不是忘了，是眼睛还没看到后面。她换慢一点的版本，让我先听完整句，再跟着唱。我拿手机录下来，唱完我们并排坐着听，找到两处容易跟丢的地方。我在纸上画好记号，喝一口已经凉了的茶，问现在能不能再试。她说先把开头读一遍，我只好把杯子放回去。',"As the rhythm sped up, the screen moved on while I was still halfway through the line. Lin An stopped the music and asked me to restart at the unfinished-words line. I read it from the page: I hadn't forgotten it; my eyes hadn't reached the ending. She chose a slower version for me to hear the full sentence, then sing along. I recorded it, and we sat together to find two places where I lost pace. After marking the page I sipped cold tea and asked to try again. Read the opening first, she said. I put the cup back down.")},
'-paired-reading':{
7:('后来陈宇唱给以前的自己，我在门外脚步后停半拍，唱给那个离开的朋友。两段录完，我们把手机放在桌边，一人拿一份稿子听。陈宇说我的那遍把留拖得太长，我正想再听，录音里给我两个字已经跟后面的声音挤在一起。我把那一处圈起来，重唱一次，把留唱短一些。他这回能接着唱到窗下那句，听完问是不是还想留第一遍。我说也有一点喜欢，先别删。他把两份分别写上日期和名字，让我明天回来再选。',"Chen Yu sang to his former self; I paused half a beat after the footsteps and sang to the departing friend. We put the phone on the table and listened with a lyric sheet each. I'd stretched 留 too long, he said. On playback, 给我 crowded into the following sounds. I circled the spot and sang again with a shorter 留. This time he could sing on to the window line. Did I still want the first take? I liked something about it too; don't delete it yet. He labelled both with the date and our names so I could choose tomorrow.")}},
6:{'-paired-reading':{
2:('林安把二十到三十写成提高百分之十，我让她拿计算器再看一下。比例是增加十个百分点，相对原来的百分之二十则增加百分之五十。她看着两个结果，说这回得把比较的是哪一个写在旁边。我们在表里留了原来的二十、后来的三十，又把人次和比例分开。改完以后，她把表发给我，问这样还会不会读错，我让她先把标题补上。',"Lin An wrote twenty to thirty as a ten-percent increase. We checked the calculator: ten percentage points, or fifty percent relative to the original twenty percent. She said we'd better label the comparison. We kept the old twenty and new thirty and separated counts from proportions. Sending the revised table, she asked whether it could still be misread. First add the headings, I said."),
7:('我们约好周四交修改方案，两周结束通报结果。我把还没确认的几项放在表后面，林安看完又加了谁负责回复这一行。有人建议连活动内容和收费也一起改，她先记在另一页，说这次把邀请做完再谈。我原来还怕周四来不及，现在看见准备、发送和确认都有了名字，就开始整理自己要问的那几个问题。她走到门口又回头，提醒我别忘了把新版表发给大家。',"We agreed to submit the revised plan Thursday and report results after two weeks. I put unresolved items at the end; Lin An added who would handle replies. Suggestions to change the activities and pricing went on another page for later. I'd feared the deadline, but with names assigned to preparation, sending and confirmation I could organise my questions. At the door she reminded me to send everyone the revised table.")}},
7:{'-d':{
9:('先问问谁搬过袋子吧，我也过去看看。',"Let's ask who moved the bag. I'll go and look too.")},
'-r':{
1:('陈宇来了以后先把蓝袋子找到，放进去五页新稿子，接着去搬桌子。我当时在活动桌旁帮人找书，只看到他从门口走过，没有看到他放纸。后来他问袋子在哪，我还说不是在你手里吗。他伸出两只空手给我看，又指向刚搬完的桌子。我这才想起来，早上还的时候是空袋子，他现在找的却已经装了今天要排的新段落。',"Chen Yu found the blue bag, put five new manuscript pages inside and went to move tables. I was helping someone find a book and saw him pass, not insert the pages. Asked where the bag was, I thought he had it. He held out empty hands and pointed at the tables he'd moved. The bag I'd returned empty now held today's new rehearsal section."),
2:('我们先问门口几个人，有人说不用的东西都到地下室去了。我正要过去，陈宇问他有没有见到蓝袋子。那个人说没有，只是以前活动常放在那里。我停下来给负责场地的人打电话，他说今天地下室没有开，先找楼上。陈宇已经走到楼道，叫我过去看，一张稿纸掉在地上，页码正好是四，上面还有他刚改过的字。',"Someone near the entrance suggested the basement, where things had gone at previous events. Before I went, Chen asked if he'd seen the blue bag. He hadn't. The venue contact told me the basement was closed today and suggested upstairs. Chen called from the corridor: a page lay on the floor, numbered four, with his latest corrections on it.")},
'-paired-reading':{
4:('志愿者说搬到二楼时，我终于松口气。他以为袋子也是活动物品，和两只纸箱一起搬走，好让入口空出来。他说纸露在袋口，我想起自己放完以后没有拉好，就请他带我们上去。楼梯那边已经堆了几箱书，我们侧着身走过，找到最里面的蓝袋子。我先打开看，林安拿着楼道捡到的那张纸站在旁边，等我把页码排好。',"The volunteer said he'd moved it upstairs with two boxes to clear the entrance. Paper had stuck out; I remembered not closing the bag. We followed him past boxes of books on the stairs to the blue bag at the back. I opened it while Lin An held the page found in the corridor, waiting for me to order the pages."),
5:('袋子里只有四张，我又紧张起来，把一到三放在一起，再找到第五页。林安递来楼道那张，正好是四，新的那一段总算连上了。纸上多了一道折痕，我把它放在桌边慢慢压平，还是有点心疼原稿。志愿者问还能不能读，我说能，都找齐了，先拿去排练吧，晚上回家再把这张夹进书里。',"There were only four pages in the bag. I found one to three and five, then Lin An handed me four from the corridor; the new section was complete. I pressed a fresh crease flat against the table, still disappointed about the original. Was it readable? Yes, everything was there. We'd rehearse now, and I'd press it inside a book at home later.")}},
8:{'-r':{
2:('陈宇问我，那新主持人到底做得怎么样。我说很喜欢他上次那个问题：在哪一刻改变了对主角的看法。我一下就想起车站那场戏，也想听旁边的人怎么说。陈宇说他也是，不过刚才在群里写得太急，把大家都愿意聊放了进去。他打开手机，改成自己很想继续那场讨论，又问我要不要一起报名。我说先看看结束时间，别又聊到赶不上车。',"Chen Yu asked what I thought of the new host. I loved his question about when our view of the protagonist changed; it brought back the station scene, and I wanted others' reactions. Chen did too, but he'd hastily written that everyone wanted to talk. He changed his message to his own wish to continue, then asked if I'd sign up. First check the finish time, I said, so I wouldn't miss the bus again.")},
'-paired-reading':{
2:('我们后来把试点写成一张很短的说明，放映仍按原来的方式进行，讨论另算名额，因为小房间坐不下所有看电影的人。愿意留下的可以在报名时勾一下，想先听也行。结束时间写九点四十五，场馆十点关门。陈宇看了看中间的十五分钟，我让他试着收完这些椅子，再检查设备。他走了一圈回来，说明白了，这段还真不能拿来继续聊。',"Our short notice kept the usual screening, with separate discussion places because the small room couldn't seat everyone. People could sign up to stay, including just to listen. Discussion ended at 9:45 and the venue closed at ten. Chen looked at the fifteen-minute gap. I asked him to try putting away the chairs and checking equipment; after a circuit of the room he agreed we couldn't use that time for more conversation.")}}
}
apply_bag_edits(EDITS)
apply(6,EDITS,'Bag actions v2: Retained genuine calculation and workplace-review text types while replacing boilerplate with actual spreadsheet revision, task assignments and a lost-bag search. Singing dialogue now offers slower practice/recording, not abstract guarantees. Both bag narrators now describe handling books, asking volunteers, ordering pages and rehearsing instead of repeatedly lecturing on evidence. Lin An returns the empty bag; Chen Yu inserts the pages and leaves its opening unclosed. Rehearsal now explicitly raises page four for everyone to see instead of inheriting the unrelated huǎng reading for a shaking action; its obsolete 晃 glossary aid is removed. The early empty-bag cue and paired narration explicitly describe placing it by the entrance, removing a misleading hái-labelled return action while retaining its time contrast and practised reply. Recovery preserves five unique pages, missing fourth page, upstairs storeroom, crease and intact new section; later copies do not end future borrowing. Film discussion retains separate sign-up and 9:45/10 cleanup; reply/attendance counts remain separate. Native flags: 风留下来 joke, 原稿心疼, 台词丢了 banter, 跟唱 omissions and calculator/percentage-point register.',glosses=[('摇头',"shake one's head"),('摸','touch; feel with a hand'),('盏','classifier for lamps'),('情绪','mood; emotion'),('计算器','calculator'),('人次','person-visits; counted attendances'),('侧','side; turn sideways'),('拉好','close or pull into place'),('压平','press flat'),('心疼','feel distressed about something valued'),('折痕','crease'),('稿纸','manuscript paper'),('楼梯','stairs'),('设备','equipment'),('傍晚','towards evening; dusk'),('逼','force; pressure someone'),('堆','pile; stack'),('盯','watch fixedly; stare at'),('盯着','keep watching'),('交还','return; hand back'),('袋口','opening of a bag'),('稿子','draft; script'),('台词','lines spoken in a play'),('腾出','make room; free up'),('纸箱','cardboard box'),('背包','backpack'),('打印','print'),('副','copy; auxiliary'),('叠','stack; pile'),('页码','page number'),('捡','pick up'),('压','press'),('厚','thick'),('夹','put between; hold between'),('空箱子','empty box')],publish='--publish' in sys.argv,omit_unused_glosses=('晃',),conversation_edits={7:{0:('林安早上放下的是空袋子，说明陈宇后来没放纸吗？','Lin An left an empty bag there in the morning. Does that mean Chen Yu never added pages later?')}})

